{"title":"Career Roadmap · Packaging Technologist","role":"Packaging Technologist","summary":"A Packaging Technologist in the food industry designs, evaluates, tests, and improves packaging systems that protect food products, preserve shelf life, maintain quality, support transportation, and meet safety, regulatory, sustainability, and commercial requirements.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Food Processing Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Packaging Technologist in the food industry designs, evaluates, tests, and improves packaging systems that protect food products, preserve shelf life, maintain quality, support transportation, and meet safety, regulatory, sustainability, and commercial requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"The role sits at the intersection of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Food science"},{"text":"Food processing"},{"text":"Packaging materials"},{"text":"Packaging engineering"},{"text":"Shelf-life science"},{"text":"Quality and food safety"},{"text":"Materials testing"},{"text":"Supply chain"},{"text":"Sustainability"},{"text":"Product development"},{"text":"Packaging machinery and automation"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["A strong profile combines food technology","packaging materials","packaging design","food safety","shelf-life analysis","testing","sustainability","data analysis."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech/B.E. Food Processing Technology","Food Chemistry + Microbiology + Processing","Packaging Materials & Packaging Science","Food–Package Interaction","Packaging Design + Testing","Barrier Properties + Shelf-Life Studies","Packaging Machinery + Filling/Sealing","Quality + Food Safety + Regulatory Knowledge","Sustainable Packaging + Cost Optimization","Packaging Development Internship","Packaging Technolo